-    => pairsTail((K -Int pyMod(K, 2)) /Int 2,
-                 neighborMin(P, N, oneRow(P, N), oneCol(P, N)))
+    => valSeqConcat(
+         pairSuffix((K -Int pyMod(K, 2)) /Int 2,
+                    neighborMin(P, N, oneRow(P, N), oneCol(P, N))),
+         vCons(1, .ValSeq))
     requires pyMod(K, 2) =/=Int 0
 
   // -----------------------------------------------------------------------

codex
The generalized-prefix shape now reaches the right circularity but the equality-style postcondition still drives a multi-gigabyte implication search. I’ve stopped that run before it threatens the new limit. I’m tightening the same invariant so its destination is a single `completePairs(A, remaining, M)` functional term whose one-step equation exactly mirrors the two executed appends; this removes the expensive relational equality while retaining the generalized mid-loop claim required by the benchmark.
apply patch
