codex
The depth-bounded residual confirms the only remaining bottleneck is arithmetic inversion of the increasing `p`/fixed `C` pair at the circularity. I’m making an equivalent implementation-level normalization: decrement `pairs` to zero. The output and complexity are unchanged, but the loop invariant now has one symbolic counter `R`, so one body step instantiates the recursive claim as `R - 1` directly.
apply patch
