codex
The fixed one-iteration probe isolated the stall further: `append` calls `valSeqConcat(A, [v])`, and the backend is recursively case-splitting the symbolic native prefix `A` without bound. The benchmark explicitly permits a guarded functional lemma for exactly this kind of stuck symbolic collection access. I’m adding `snocVS(A,v)` as the structurally defined singleton-concat selector and simplifying only `valSeqConcat(A, vCons(v,.ValSeq))`; it does not bypass either append or any heap write.
